CI/CD through github actions and deploy a static website on AWS S3 Bucket

Create a new repo and add index.html file 
Create IAM -> Git settings Secret and variables -> Give access key and id
Create s3 bucket and give permissions 
In git workflows main.yml write the script

name: Upload Website
 
on:
  push:
    branches:
    - main
 
jobs:
  deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
    - name: Checkout
      uses: actions/checkout@v1
 
    - name: Configure AWS Credentials
      uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@v1
      with:
        aws-access-key-id: ${{ secrets.AWS_ACCESS_KEY }}
        aws-secret-access-key: ${{ secrets.AWS_SECRET_KEY }}
        aws-region: us-east-1
 
    - name: Deploy static site to S3 bucket
      run: aws s3 sync ./ s3://hellooooo12 [S3 Bucket name]

